  "rationale": "Evidence from iteration 7 (score 499.5, down from 619.4): the oval still completes 20/20 (progress 0.998, rms 0.009, 2.06 s), so the higher kp/kd helped tracking there. The s-bend fell from 18/20 finishes to 7/20. Its oscillation rose from 0.48 to 0.35 in the other direction and its control effort reached 24, so kp 6.5 with kd 1.0 is overcorrecting on bends. The slalom did not move: progress was 0.16-0.17 at kp 4, 5.3 and 6.5, with 0-1 line-loss events per run and max_error at the 0.06 m floor. Gain and speed changes have therefore not limited slalom, and the likely cause is tape coverage on sharp weaves, as iteration 7's own notes suggested. Changes: (1) revert kp from 6.5 to 5.3 and kd from 1.0 to 0.8, the iteration-6 setting that gave the best s-bend result, to recover the bend finishes; (2) raise sensor_size from 0.012 to 0.016 so each footprint covers more of the 25 mm tape and the signal stays valid on sharp weaves. With spacing 0.027 m the 16 mm footprints still overlap, and the signal stays a lateral-offset estimate; (3) keep base_speed 0.75, ki 1.0, geometry (except sensor size) and last_direction unchanged, so the effect is isolated. Expected result: s-bend back to about 16-18 of 20 finishes, oval still completing, and slalom progress rising above 0.3 if coverage was the limit. Hypotheses: (a) slalom progress exceeds 0.3 with the larger footprint; (b) s-bend finish rate returns to at least 80%; (c) steering_oscillation stays below 0.35 on all tracks. If slalom stays flat, the next lever is a wider sensor span or a lower base_speed on the weaves, not kp.",
